  <title id="bdl04imdbparallel-title">Test accuracy and negative log-likelihood of parallel SMC and HMC on IMDb</title>
  <desc id="bdl04imdbparallel-desc">Left panel, at a budget of about 10,000 epochs, against R from 1 to 8 on a log scale: SMC parallel accuracy rises from 88.60 to 88.72 percent and its NLL falls from 0.2856 to 0.2846, while HMC parallel and serial HMC stay near 88.68 to 88.71 percent accuracy and an NLL of about 0.2854. Right panel, R equal to 8, against a wall-clock budget of 40, 700 and 10,000 epochs on a log scale: SMC parallel and HMC parallel collapse to about 83 percent accuracy with an NLL above 0.6 at 40 epochs, reach about 87 percent and an NLL of 0.32 at 700 epochs, and converge to 88.7 percent and 0.28 at 10,000 epochs, where serial HMC, which stays near 88.3 to 88.7 percent throughout, also ends.</desc>
